- Visual inspection: PASS for pages 21--25 (affected pages plus the preceding
  and following pages).  Text, equations, figure, caption, and page breaks are
  legible; no clipping or overlap was observed.
- Duplicate PDF check: manuscript/manuscript.pdf and ./manuscript.pdf have the
  same SHA-256 hash after synchronization.

Warnings and unresolved assumptions
-----------------------------------
- The first manual verifier run caught and corrected two draft algebra errors:
  P_yy(-1,-3/2)=6 and disc_y P=-4(8e^3+27).
- An early LaTeX run caught malformed inline delimiters in the new subsection;
  the source was corrected and the final build succeeds.
- The accessible Fedoryuk preview verifies chapter/section titles and starting
  pages, but not exact theorem numbering or full theorem hypotheses.  No
  theorem numbers are asserted.
- A global canonical-domain chain has not been constructed.  Uniform close-
  pair matching, possible Airy passage at the remaining simple point, pole
  endpoint control, sheet/logarithm monodromy, and equivalence with the entire
  Bargmann germ remain open.
- No identification C_ess=0 iff Delta_WI=0 is used or proved.
- Numerical Stokes tracing is illustrative verification only, not proof of
  global connectivity.

Outcome
-------
Outcome A: proved sectorial Fedoryuk theorem.  Away from the pole and turning
points, deliberately chosen canonical domains meet the local meromorphic WKB
hypotheses, and standard local simple- and close/double-turning-point
constructions identify the necessary descriptions.  Outcomes B and C are not
justified because the physical global chain and its Bargmann identification
remain unproved.

